## (5) what the new channel reads (and what it does not)

Per ~100 ms tick, `capture_thread_state` does, in this order:
  GetThreadTimes + GetProcessTimes        (no suspend, no context — pure counters)
  SuspendThread                           (returns the previous suspend count)
  GetThreadContext                        (CONTEXT: Rip, Rsp — read only)
  ResumeThread                            (only if SuspendThread succeeded)
Nothing in it raises; a failure becomes `err=` text on the sample line. No WriteProcessMemory, no
patchCode, no hook, no Interceptor, no Memory.protect, no new export in the DLL. `rip` is classified
against the DLL's own image span (PE SizeOfImage from the loaded module) so "inside_dll" means the
thread was executing our artifact's code.

